==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 40~80 seconds<sup>1,200f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60~80 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring either a Freeze Up (M) combo [[Cat Combo]] ([[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!!]]) or two Freeze Up (Sm) Combos, along with [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]— this is potent enough for a single Bombercat to perma-Freeze [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]]. Add a group of [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer attackers]], and then your standard meatshields.

Your goal is to carry a Bombercat safely to Le'noir before the first [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] resurfaces from its tunnel (which can be done by sending out two Bombercats as soon as you can afford them). If Bombercat Freezes Le'noir, he will not break free as he has only 1 knockback, and the Zombies will simply burrow without harming Bomber. Once the first Zombie resurfaces, it becomes difficult to Freeze Le'noir in the future. Note that a resurfacing Zoge may be able to kill your Bombercat(s) due to his high range. However, if you use [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] instead (requires a Freeze Up (M) and a Freeze Up (Sm)), then the Zoge will burrow far enough to not kill Healer.

Once Le'noir is permanently Frozen, you can send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to shred through Le'noir's health pool in just a few attack cycles. Once he's dead the stage is effectively won, as you will only need to stall the burrowing Zombies while Awakened Bahamut destroys the base. Feel free to add other rushers like [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] to expedite the process.

==Trivia==
*Wandering Conch's Japanese name, Sasurai no Horagai (さすらいのホラガイ, "Wandering Conch"), may be a pun on the ''[https://youtu.be/z7AciJ5LwS0 Sasurai no Naisu Gai]'' (さすらいのナイスガイ, "Wandering Nice Guy") story from the game ''[[wikipedia:Power Pro Kun Pocket|Power Pro Kun Pocket 9]]''.

